<title>USA: ADR REPORT - Nokia up on merger rumours.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - Nokia up on merger rumours.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Nokia Group were up in trading on the New York Stock Exchange on market rumors that it was planning to merge with telecommunications rival Telefon AB L.M. Ericsson.</p>
<p>Nokia was up 3-3/8 at 57-3/8 on the NYSE while Ericsson was up 1-3/8 at 30-1/4. Both companies quickly denied the rumors and market players in Stockholm said they doubted there was any basis to it.</p>
<p>Among Latin American shares, stock of Brazilian telecoms giant Telebras rose 3/4 at 76-1/8 on the NYSE. Two brokerages reiterated strong buy ratings.</p>
